b that I went to my friend  that something needs to change here it  was a real turning point for me because  I would just stay up at night crying I  had no idea what to do I was like  they're going to evict me soon and my  friend of like you should go to  financial teeth University I'm Dorothy  bridges and I'm an FPU coordinator petty  and the first night of our class she  came in and she set right up front in  the corner and I'll never forget because  we finished the class and the way  everywhere everyone had left adding a  still setting there and she was crying  she was in tears and saying that there  was no way she could do this and get out  of this because she was in such a mess  it really made me confront exactly what  was going on in my life mine hit rock  bottom it would be five thousand dollars  even get called up and I don't have five  thousand dollars how my folks save a  thousand dollars I I don't think I  really told anybody how bad it was until  I was at the club and so I asked her I  said just give us nine weeks give us  nine weeks and we're going to work with  you and we're going to walk with you and  so I asked her to go home that night and  I said I want you to sit down and right  where you are right now and how you're  feeling and I said them in nine weeks  from now when we finished let's see  where you are  let's compare because I said I think  you're going to find yourself in a much  different place I didn't miss one class  I was like I have to go to this every  single week because I knew I was just  been so much trouble I'm like I got it  just give this at all that I have at the  moment and the more I did the more I  followed the program the more things  just started happening in my life that  really worked out in the time of the  class I paid off nine thousand dollars  in nine weeks  which was really exciting if anyone and  told me I would do that I would both  laugh and said you are crazy  I haven't even made $9,000 those years  but I did so at the end of the nine we  always ask for class members to share  with us and what they've learned and  what they've gained through the class  and who she was in tears but it was much  different this time it was that first  Mikey who tears of joy relief of hope  that she you know she finally had some  hope and that she saw that she could do  it and she had the tools to do it so I  guess it's been about three or four  months since I took the class and I  haven't paid off all my credit cards yet  but I'm very very close to getting my  consumer debt done with my  projectionists to pay off around thirty  five thousand dollars and a little over  a year which is exciting with student  loans I have approximately one hundred  and fifty thousand dollars a semi nice  house or condo here in Nashville and  when I've looked at it if I were to stay  in my same salary level I'll have all my  student loans paid off in five years  [Music]

